<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belmopan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belmopan is the capital of Belize, a planned city built in the interior of the country in the 1960s. The government decided to move the capital from coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belize-city">Belize City</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-hattie">Hurricane Hattie</a> devastated it in 1961, and Belmopan became the seat of government in 1970. It remains much smaller than Belize City.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belmopan.jpg" alt="Belmopan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CadabraPuppet · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Assembly_Building,_Belize.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
